<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian official reserves rise in April.</title>
<headline>Australian official reserves rise in April.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's holdings of gold and foreign exchange assets rose to US$17.37 billion in April from US$17.12 billion in March, compared with US$14.00 billion in April 1996, the Reserve Bank of Australia said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In Australian dollar terms, reserves rose by A$463 million to A$22.23 billion in April from A$21.77 billion in March compared with A$17.82 billion a year earlier, the bank said.</p>
<p>The bank said that all of the April increase was due to valuation effects.  </p>
<p>Individual reserve assets in Australian dollars were -</p>
<p>			     Apr 1997	  Mch 1997	 Apr 1996</p>
<p>    Gold		3.44 billion    3.50 billion   3.94 billion</p>
<p>    SDRs		  39 million	40 million     63 million</p>
<p>IMF Reserve position</p>
<p>			   585 million     587 million    625 million</p>
<p>Foreign Exchange</p>
<p>			 18.17 billion   17.65 billion  13.20 billion</p>
<p>    TOTAL:	   22.23 billion   21.77 billion  17.82 billion</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
